    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>A computer network is a group of computers connected together to communicate and share resources, such as internet connections, printers, or files.</p><h3>Why Do We Need Networks?</h3><p>Without networks, transferring files would require physical media like USB drives. Networks enable instant communication, centralized data management, and the modern internet.</p><h3>Practical Example</h3><p>Your home Wi-Fi is a network. It connects your phone, laptop, and smart TV to a central router, which then connects to the global internet.</p>
        </div>
        
